    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.4 rule 3 (formerly `eager_target_bearing`). Two match-less templates: `deriv_c` carries a spatial `D` in its body, `scale_c` does not. Both references survive load. The `central` rule applies inside `deriv_c`'s body for its one instance and writes a reference to itself (§9.6.3 constraint 7), so `deriv_c`'s body is rewritten in place to `ref(central, {f: f})` and `central` materializes as a match-less entry in its authored position (§9.6.4 rule 5); `scale_c` is unchanged. `expanded.esm` is the fully lowered tree the eager-expansion engine produced, and stays the Expand oracle.",
    "name": "rewrite_in_template_body"
  },
